  "reason": "slate from its quarries and wool from the summer pastures, sawn timber from the valley's larches; the drovers' inn on the Garth Road; it sends slate, timber and wool down to Cogsworth. Its old trade over the north pass stopped when the Starfall brought the rockfall down; the road beyond waits for a later region",
  "terrain": "a sheltered valley on the upper Cog inside the range: stepped streets on the east bank, stone houses on retaining walls, steep wooded slopes and snow on the peaks round it",
  "fit": "the town steps up its terraces on retaining walls: each street on one tier, a stair or a ramp between",
